        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T00:31:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That does not really prevent someone from making a mistake. Another way could be to use the reference instead of the pointer.",
      "parentUuid": "bc2af0aa_c278a576",
      "revId": "6e3662d54d90671fe1c6d23340004df871cdfb84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba1888f0_7d2a1137",
        "filename": "android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 490,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T00:36:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please don\u0027t mark a comment as resolved if you disagree with it.\n\n\u003e That does not really prevent someone from making a mistake.\n\nYes indeed, but I prefer it to crash loudly than silently hide the mistake.\n\ngo/error-handling-smells#defensive-programming\n\n\u003e Another way could be to use the reference instead of the pointer.\n\nWorks for me, but this sounds like a bigger change.",
      "parentUuid": "a6ad50b9_ce088235",
      "revId": "6e3662d54d90671fe1c6d23340004df871cdfb84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f45c3181_43341e3d",
        "filename": "android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 490,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T18:30:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m happy for this one to be an assert or to skip the check.",
      "parentUuid": "ba1888f0_7d2a1137",
      "revId": "6e3662d54d90671fe1c6d23340004df871cdfb84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ceb361b1_57e9901c",
        "filename": "android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T00:19:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the definition of `bdname` it\u0027s an array of `249` byte, so 1 more than the Bluetooth limit.\n\nAre we sure it can be not null terminated?",
      "revId": "6e3662d54d90671fe1c6d23340004df871cdfb84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0350cc85_3f1d794a",
        "filename": "android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T00:31:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_dm.cc?q\u003dsymbol%3A%5Cbbtif_dm_ssp_cfm_req_evt%5Cb%20case%3Ayes\n\nIt is possible that the string is not null terminated.\n\nHere I am trying to make sure that we don\u0027t run into problems due to mistakes in other places.",
      "parentUuid": "ceb361b1_57e9901c",
      "revId": "6e3662d54d90671fe1c6d23340004df871cdfb84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c928d12_dec01a12",
        "filename": "android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T00:36:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This sounds like a bug, especially since `BD_NAME_LEN` is `248`, so the last byte value is undefined.",
      "parentUuid": "0350cc85_3f1d794a",
      "revId": "6e3662d54d90671fe1c6d23340004df871cdfb84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ab2d853_65f98d22",
        "filename": "android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T00:36:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to check it, I would prefer for you to add an assert instead and make the stack crash if `bdname-\u003ename` is not null terminated`",
      "parentUuid": "5c928d12_dec01a12",
      "revId": "6e3662d54d90671fe1c6d23340004df871cdfb84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "debb25ac_7e51e717",
        "filename": "android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T18:30:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have any problem with setting the last character to 0.  It makes sense to me, and it is very little overhead.  Minimizing how much of the stack we change with each CL reduces risk.",
      "parentUuid": "2ab2d853_65f98d22",
      "revId": "6e3662d54d90671fe1c6d23340004df871cdfb84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
